CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ alias in namespace: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member declarator in namespace: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ parameter in namespace: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ block scope: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Classes declared by elaborated-type-specifiers used to go into the global
scope (and, from an alias template, into none until its first use), so
N::tag, N::inner_ref and N::param_t were not members of N.
